    "text": "1 days ago MONROE COUNTY, Ga. — The Monroe County Commission voted unanimously Tuesday to censure one of its members after an outside investigation found credible evidence he made racially offensive remarks to county employees — including asking about renting a county-owned gazebo for a \"lynching\" and suggesting two female employees should \"own one or two\" Black people. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
